## Coverage gate added

File: .github/workflows/swift-production.yml
Job:  coverage-gate

### What the job does

1. Runs: go test -cover -coverprofile=coverage.out ./scheme/swift/stable/...
2. Reports total statement coverage via go tool cover -func
3. Lists all 0%-coverage functions in stable.go
4. Subtracts EXEMPT=2 (known dead-code entries)
5. Reports non-exempt zero-coverage function count
6. Uploads coverage.out as artifact (retention 14 days)
7. Exits 0 (soft gate — will be hardened once C2 remediation is complete for all rules)

### Gate status

SOFT (exit 0 unconditionally)

Rationale: 2 dead-code functions remain at 0% and are exempt; flipping to
hard gate (exit $live_zero) requires either removing the dead code or
adding per-function exemption tracking.  Current non-exempt zero count = 0.

### Known dead-code exemptions (documented in coverage.go)

  scheme/swift/stable/stable.go:5003: extractConstraintSig
  scheme/swift/stable/stable.go:9724: renderIndexSubset

These are tracked in internal/coverage/swift_grammar/coverage.go as
KnownDeadCode + PrintDeadCodeNote.

### Trigger conditions

Same as existing apple-corpus job:
  - push to main (paths: scheme/swift/stable/**, .github/workflows/swift-production.yml)
  - pull_request (same paths)
  - schedule (nightly 02:00 UTC)
  - workflow_dispatch

### pr-summary dependency

coverage-gate added to needs: [apple-corpus, production-parity, coverage-gate]
in the pr-summary job so the summary waits for coverage results.

